{
  "about": [
    "Sizes of shipped payloads that cross a host or guest transport, against that transport's limit.",
    "Checked by transport-payload-budgets.test.ts. The top of host-transport-size-limits.test.ts says which test proves each limit, and which limits belong to Proxmox or Windows and are not checked by Hivra's code.",
    "Each payload must stay within budgetFraction of its limit unless overBudget names it with a reason.",
    "After an intended change: UPDATE_TRANSPORT_BUDGETS=1 npx jest src/lib/services/__tests__/transport-payload-budgets.test.ts"
  ],
  "budgetFraction": 0.75,
  "limits": {
    "linux-argument": {
      "bytes": 131071,
      "what": "One argument to exec on Linux: MAX_ARG_STRLEN is 131,072 bytes including the NUL. Applies to every argv word on the host (python3 -c, qm guest exec, ssh) and in a Linux guest."
    },
    "host-script-with-stdin.script": {
      "bytes": 98259,
      "what": "runProxmoxHostScriptWithStdin: the largest script whose base64 login command is still one Linux argument (the 96 KiB script check never binds first)."
    },
    "host-script-with-stdin.stdin": {
      "bytes": 1048576,
      "what": "runProxmoxHostScriptWithStdin: stdin, counted in UTF-8 bytes."
    },
    "guest-exec-stdin": {
      "bytes": 1048576,
      "what": "Proxmox qm guest exec --pass-stdin forwards at most 1 MiB to the guest agent."
    },
    "sudo-transport-script": {
      "bytes": 999999,
      "what": "runProxmoxHostScript on a user's server with a sudo login: the loader's length prefix allows 999,999 bytes of script. A root login (the managed fleet) sends the script to bash -s with no limit."
    },
    "provider-guest-seed": {
      "bytes": 1048576,
      "what": "runProviderGuestSeed: the largest guest seed script sent over a provider VM's enrolled SSH pin."
    },
    "windows-command-line": {
      "bytes": 32766,
      "what": "Windows CreateProcess: 32,767 characters including the NUL. qemu-ga starts powershell.exe through GLib, whose spawn helper adds its own arguments, so real headroom is a little lower."
    },
    "cloud-init-user-data": {
      "bytes": 32768,
      "what": "Hetzner Cloud user_data limit, also renderFirstBootCloudInit's own check."
    }
  },
  "overBudget": {
    "windows-rdp-preparation commandLine": "Measured, not yet run on a Windows guest: the whole PowerShell program is one -EncodedCommand argument (UTF-16LE base64, about 2.7 characters per program character), so about 460 more program characters would pass Windows' command-line limit. Owner follow-up: send the program on stdin as windows-rdp-capability does.",
    "bankr-skills proxmoxHostScript": "Only on a user's server with a sudo login (the managed fleet uses bash -s with no limit). The skill files are base64 twice and not compressed; the provider-VM lane gzips the same suite to 27%. Owner follow-up: compress it here too."
  },
